  "core_idea": "Research with marginalised communities should serve human rights and social justice. Realities are shaped by power and privilege, so the researcher works with the community, attends to whose version of reality is accepted, and designs the study to support change.",
  "key_concepts_note": "Use the concepts already stored for this theory in the library (theories.concepts).",
  "when_to_use": [
    "Research with groups that face discrimination or exclusion.",
    "Evaluation of programmes where power differences shape results.",
    "Typical designs: participatory and mixed-methods designs with community involvement at each stage."
  ],
  "common_mistakes": [
    "Naming the paradigm without involving the community in the design.",
    "Treating it as a method; it is a set of assumptions that guides any method.",
    "Assuming the researcher knows what change the community wants."
  ],
